<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore April M1 rises 4.4 pct yr on year - MAS.</title>
<headline>Singapore April M1 rises 4.4 pct yr on year - MAS.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Money supply figures.</p>
<p>	   (in billions of Singapore dollars)</p>
<p>			     April 97  March 97  April 96</p>
<p>M-1 (narrow money)	 27.67   28.47     26.49</p>
<p>M-2			   118.22   117.03    105.81</p>
<p>M-3 (broad money)	 146.97   145.10    132.25</p>
<p>Demand deposits	    17.05   17.74     16.43</p>
<p>Currency in active	 10.62   10.73     10.06</p>
<p>circulation</p>
<p>Note - The Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS) said narrow money supply (M1) grew by 4.4 percent year-on-year in April, compared with 9.8 percent in March.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)  </p>
